  "body": "## Summary\n\nDependent integration after #408, incorporating the inspected #331 head `35a92e04b1f3f1a7def3f9c126d19cde3d00b5c3` and default main `d4bd497df`.\n\nPreserve all downstream payment/callback/refund recovery protections. Add merchant-bound routing, recurring completion gates, flow-scoped transfer configuration, unpaid contact-only marketplace coordination, and environment-separated financial reporting. Reconcile the upstream refund SQL trigger with the application ledger writer; assertions count both history event types to detect double accounting.\n\nSee `docs/payments/stack-integration-2026-09-16.md` for pinned inputs, conflict decisions, exact test commands, initial failures, blockers, and rollback. Companion mobile PR: https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/88. Mobile head `ff77c2060034762f69aed81473c8f94a25684d7e` is pushed before this gitlink.\n\n## Tests completed locally\n\n- Backend: 2,674 examples PASS.\n- Real PostgreSQL provider/refund integration with new trigger: 249 examples PASS.\n- Real PostgreSQL merchant/contact/report boundaries: 4 examples PASS.\n- Canonical migrations, historical refund backfill, replay, constraint rejection and preservation-only rollback: PASS on isolated PostgreSQL 16.\n- Native migration runner rejects populated databases and URL overrides before writes.\n- Mobile lint/types and 458 tests / 78 suites PASS.\n- Focused admin/refund/access web tests: 41 PASS.\n- Previously timed-out course-admin suite: 626 tests PASS on unchanged rerun.\n- Full web lint and build/bundle budget PASS (314,065 gzip initial bytes, five preloads).\n- Repo quality PASS; production-release 60 and CI-policy 23 tests PASS.\n- Strict catalog inventory regeneration PASS; no exemptions or relaxed gate.\n\nHosted web quality for code commit `60fe0aea06b9153b953005290ecc8ba9659c04aa` PASSED: **2,089 tests / 217 suites**, 203.867s; completed 2026-09-16T20:12:35Z. Evidence: https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35144435997/job/104956908672. Hosted mobile quality, API contracts, migrations, repo quality, catalog authority and persona browser journeys also passed; backend CI was still in progress. New checks on the final documentation-only head may remain pending.\n\nDo not hide the local failures: the first full web run failed in the course suite amid a disk-full log error, and an isolated reproduction began with a 15-second timeout and cascading React act failures. The unchanged course suite subsequently passed all 626 tests. The duplicate slow full-web rerun was stopped after verifying hosted success: **exit 143**, 82 passing / four failing suites recorded, not a local full-suite pass. Initial mobile permission assertion failed before canonical-policy reconciliation; final mobile 458/458 passed. No assertion, timeout or quality gate was relaxed.\n\n## Migration / rollout warning\n\nReuse the upstream additive `2026-09-16_payment_intent_refund_sync.sql` unchanged. It backfills existing succeeded intent-bound refund records; this is not fresh provider verification. Production-shaped historical reconciliation and qualified operator/legal/accounting review are mandatory before activation. Rollback removes synchronization code only and retains financial balances/history; never blindly restore earlier balances. No production/staging migration was executed.\n\nNo provider activation, real provider HTTP, native device walkthrough, screenshots, staging deploy, live transaction or GitHub merge. Existing staging authentication and merchant-contract/credential qualification blockers remain. Keep flags disabled.\n\n## Review order\n\nUpdated #331 through the existing dependent chain ending #408, then this PR. Review the companion mobile integration after #85 (plus mobile main and #83 ancestry) before using the new gitlink. Draft only, no requested reviewer or merge action.\n",
